    "created_at": "2022-10-20T14:34:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-20T14:34:29Z",
    "body": "`<ellipse>` is always a whole ellipse, i.e it doesn't have to deal with *startAngle* and *endAngle*.  \r\nThe [`A`rc command](https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/paths.html#PathDataEllipticalArcCommands) would have been a better candidate, but that one uses \"endpoint parameterization\", while canvas2D uses \"center parametrization\", see [this note](https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/implnote.html#ArcImplementationNotes). I don't think we can reuse much from it to describe what's really done in canvas.",
